        <item>
            <title>Version 1.7.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:58:50 -0500</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>A new look</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>New app icon</b>, built in Icon Composer and rendered natively with Liquid Glass (no more grey legacy frame in the Dock).</li>
<li><b>Frosted title sheet</b> across the top of the window, with the logo, version, settings and Check Now.</li>
<li><b>Sections are floating panels</b> that roll smoothly open and closed. Each has its own <i>Update</i> button, and remembers whether you collapsed it.</li>
<li>Cards keep a fixed size and reflow with the window; the default window fits three across.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Updates</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>macOS updates open Software Update</b> in System Settings instead of installing directly.</li>
<li><b>App Store:</b> apps UpdateScout can update keep their own cards; only the ones that need the App Store are grouped into a single <i>Open App Store</i> card.</li>
<li>Check for updates as often as every 5 minutes.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Settings</h2>
<ul>
<li>Version and <i>Check for Updates</i> at the top of Settings, which now opens centred on the main window.</li>
<li>New <b>Glass</b> slider from Clear to Opaque, and a smooth crossfade when switching light and dark.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Fixes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Collapsing a section near the bottom no longer makes the list jump.</li>
<li>Sharper logos, a clearer password dialog, and readable section counts in dark mode.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
